<!--
    Phosphor's barbell, the same glyph and the same path data the tab bar draws from
    `src/lib/ui/icons/Barbell.svelte`. Its 256-unit viewBox is kept verbatim rather than
    rescaled, so the two stay one icon: a change in the app can be pasted straight across.

    Sized 24dp on a 48dp square because the launcher does not mask or pad a shortcut icon
    the way it does the launcher icon — what is drawn here is what appears, and a glyph
    filling its own bounds reads as too large beside the system's own entries.

    `@color/colorAccent` resolves against the *launcher's* configuration, not this app's,
    which is what makes the `-night` qualifier work here: cobalt is blue-600 on a light
    home screen and blue-500 on a dark one, exactly as it is inside the app.
-->
